From 60e5b9d331e6c0b0a41f12dfd9fac0fe828ed2f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:41:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 096/105] script: add P2MR leaf version 0xe2, whose ML-DSA-44
 checks can be disabled

Leaf version 0xe2 (P2MR_LEAF_LATTICE_TRIPWIRED, control byte 0xe3)
executes in a P2MR leaf of depth one or more as leaf version 0xc0 does,
when the new SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE flag is set: the same
tapscript rules, validation weight budget, OP_SUCCESSx pre-scan and
signature message, with the leaf version in the tapleaf hash, and
OP_CHECKMLDSA44 and OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S where their flags are set too.
Without the flag it stays an unknown leaf version, and in P2TR it is one
whatever the flags. No deployment sets the flag yet.

Such a leaf sets both m_tripwired_leaf, so that its elliptic curve checks
follow the tripwire of leaf version 0xe0 exactly (they fail with
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED), and the new m_lattice_tripwired_leaf,
false unless set, which only the P2MR branch sets. m_tripwired_leaf has a
second reader since the rescue lane: an elliptic curve check in an
executed leaf of version 0xe2 is rescuable as one in 0xe0 is, wherever
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE is not set.

The second new flag, SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED, makes
OP_CHECKMLDSA44 with any non-empty signature chunk fail the script in such
a leaf, with the new error SCRIPT_ERR_P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED ("ML-DSA-44
signature checks are disabled in this leaf"). EvalCheckMLDSA44 now takes
the flags, and the check sits after the validation weight is charged and
the public key chunks are checked, and before the signature chunks, the
hash type, the signature cache and the verifier are looked at, so OP_NOT
cannot turn the outcome around and a 520-byte chunk of any content fails
the same way. An empty signature still pushes false. No rescue token is
looked for there: the disabled ML-DSA-44 check is not rescuable in this
series. Leaf versions 0xc0 and 0xe0, OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S, P2TR, legacy and
witness v0 scripts are unaffected.

The flags take bits 27 and 28, after M4-S's 25 and M4-R's 26; their names
are P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE and P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED. The unknown bits that
formatscriptflags uses were moved above them by the rescue lane already.

The script_flags fuzz targets no longer add or remove
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE: like the other P2MR execution flags it
turns a script that DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION refuses into one
that executes. SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED only makes more scripts
fail, and is fuzzed.

p2mr_ts_m4_tests pinned 0xe2 as an unknown leaf version. Its four pq2
spends at 0xe2, signed by p2mr-ts, now execute and pass with the flag, and
are pinned as unknown without it; with SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED
the two ML-DSA-44 ones fail and the two SLH-DSA ones pass.

See doc/p2mr-lattice-tripwire.md, added later in this series.
